# The anchor_entry state - the `&` decision in an entry hole: the FIRST (or a further) bookmark
# entered on the hole's container through the same portion face a reference uses. Also documents
# the committed anchors ROWS (no other chapter covers them).
Bookmark being entered (a &-led hole)
description: the anchor_entry state, and the committed anchor rows
- >
  The hole's text begins with `&` - the BOOKMARK decision (keys.ts classifies it; yamlover
  dialect, entry stage only - in a value hole `&…` stays text, so the inline `&'p: q' v`
  spelling still types through verbatim). The body enters as the SAME portion cells a `*`
  reference uses - the scope ladder climbs on `:` in the empty first cell, segments commit on
  `:`, completion rides the active cell as the INLINE TAIL (the pointer_entry law: the armed
  candidate's untyped remainder selected in the cell, `:`/Enter/Tab accept, Escape closes the
  dropdown only, Delete discards the tail) - with
  two anchor-only differences: `[` never folds an index and POSITION hints are not offered (a
  bookmark may not claim a position - makeAnchor refuses), and a trailing `-` segment spells
  keyless membership (`: -`, the ordinal bookmark). The bookmark lands on the hole's CONTAINER -
  the own-line law: a `&: path` line attaches to the node whose block holds it. Enter joins the
  segments and parses-or-refuses through makeAnchor; a valid body commits the anchor and the
  hole RETURNS at its own index, empty - the bookmark is a decoration, no entry was born, so
  there is nothing to descend into. Backspace on the emptied floor undoes the `&` decision.
- >
  THE RECENTS BAG rides below the hints here too (the pointer_entry law - rows never arm, a
  pick INSERTS, the two-stage Escape ladder), reading the per-project `bookmarks` list - the
  SAME list the tag picker files into (a tag application IS a membership bookmark). Two
  anchor-only differences: a remembered path bearing a POSITION segment is not offered
  (makeAnchor refuses position claims), and the offered raw carries the MEMBERSHIP form -
  the trailing `: -` rides along, so the pick fills the dominant `&tag:-` gesture whole and
  Enter commits it. A committed bookmark files its TARGET (the `-` stripped) back into the
  list.
- >
  AND THE `&` BAG ALSO OFFERS THE VOCABULARY: with the remembered list short or empty, the
  project's ontos fill the rest (ontos.ts - the same tags the picker shows as chips, the
  grafted taxonomy plus the configured `settings.ontos` location). A bookmark IS a tag
  application, so the two surfaces must suggest the same words; without this a fresh project
  left the bookmark face with nothing to offer while the picker looked rich.
- !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
  header:
    - Event
      width: 2
    - 'Condition / note'
      width: 4
    - 'Next state'
      width: 2
  - ['`alphanumeric`', 'native text in the active segment cell', '`anchor_entry` (stays)']
  - ['`colon`', 'the empty first cell, ladder below world - the SCOPE CLIMBS', '`anchor_entry` (stays)']
  - ['`colon`', 'otherwise - the segment COMMITS, the next cell opens', '`anchor_entry` (stays)']
  - ['`open_bracket`', 'NO index fold - a bookmark may not claim a position; the `[` is plain text', '`anchor_entry` (stays)']
  - ['`hint_pick`', 'a dropdown row (Tab/Enter on the ARMED row, or a click) REPLACES the active cell''s text - position rows are never offered', '`anchor_entry` (stays)']
  - ['`bag_pick`', 'a recents-bag row INSERTS the remembered bookmark whole - the membership `: -` included, position-bearing paths never offered; Enter then commits', '`anchor_entry` (stays)']
  - ['`escape`', 'the two-stage ladder (pointer_entry): hints close first, the bag stands; then the bag; then the page''s law', '`anchor_entry` (stays)']
  - ['`enter`', 'the joined body is a bookmark spelling (keys walked, a trailing `-` for keyless membership) - the anchor commits on the CONTAINER and the hole returns at its own index', '[entry_hole](*::server:yamlover-editor:entry_hole)']
  - ['`enter`', 'a position claim or no body - the ring, the segments stand', '[error_flash](*::server:yamlover-editor:error_flash)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'at the head of a non-first segment - the cells MERGE at the junction', '`anchor_entry` (stays)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'the first cell''s head, ladder above bare - the SCOPE DESCENDS', '`anchor_entry` (stays)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'the emptied floor (one empty cell, bare scope) - the `&` decision undoes, the plain hole returns', '[entry_hole](*::server:yamlover-editor:entry_hole)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'otherwise', '`anchor_entry` (stays)']
- >
  The COMMITTED anchor rows (a node that already carries bookmarks) are plain text cells after
  the value - one row, one anchor, the body without its `&`. The walk reaches them as a stop;
  Enter re-commits the row in place (parses-or-refuses, the caret stays); an EMPTIED row commits
  as that anchor's removal - the last one removes the stop and the caret lands on the node; the
  trailing `+` ADD slot appends. Tab and the arrows WALK (a decoration row has no levels). On
  the wire a bookmark is IDENTITY: any anchor change re-emplaces the node wholesale (yed-sync
  identityMarks) - there is no surgical anchor facet.
